WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:05.128
Reading a quantisation claim out of the GGUF header.

00:00:05.128 --> 00:00:08.947
Four files parsed: the per-layer structure is one fixed split.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.246
The card, from PollardWeights: Bits placed by per-layer sensitivity, not a uniform crush.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.430
Low rungs, at three different bit budgets.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.903
3 of 3: same keep-set: blocks 0, 1, 63, 64.

00:00:23.903 --> 00:00:27.927
Blocks 2 to 62 flattened to IQ1_S in each.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.722
Saved by demoting two tensor groups to IQ1_S.

00:00:33.722 --> 00:00:39.563
Attn_k and attn_v, 11 MB; ffn_gate and ffn_up, 765 MB.

00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:43.067
Out of a 7.34 GB file.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.386
A fixed first-and-last rule, not a per-budget knapsack.

00:00:47.386 --> 00:00:49.471
The quality numbers deserve credit.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.858
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
